{"availability":"available","full":"timharris707/skills","name":"skills","description":"23 practical agent skills: TeamWorkflow, multi-model review, media ingestion, and writing. Original Claude Code packages plus a Codex desktop edition tuned for Astra. Source for clickai.dev.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":40,"forks":6,"created":"2026-06-25T02:24:41Z","updated":"2026-10-08T20:52:47Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://timharris707.github.io/skills/","topics":["agent-skills","ai-agents","ai-workflow","claude-code","claude-code-plugin","developer-tools","llm","multi-agent","prompt-engineering"],"demo":"https://timharris707.github.io/skills/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:56.095Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:56.095Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:56.095Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:39.306Z","stars":40,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:56.095Z","stars":40,"forks":6}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["I've led dev teams for over twenty years. I never wrote the code. These skills give me a lead developer who runs the team, so all I have to bring is the idea. Four shipped products so far.","Most of these skills started as someone else's. Fifteen are adapted from Matt Pocock's Skills For Real Engineers, three from Lauren Tan, six are mine. I rewrote nearly all of them for someone who won't read the code, then tied them together under one orchestrator session that takes the idea, decides what gets grilled, mapped, prototyped, built, and reviewed, and runs the rest. That's what lets a non-engineer ship at production quality. I talk to that one session the way I've always talked to a dev lead.","Each skill is a SKILL.md, a plain-markdown playbook the agent reads on its own: every workflow I used to re-explain each session, written down once, installed in one line and versioned like software."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https:/